<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; (this.get(i) == null) => (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i))) || (this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the assertion can be simplified to ensure it captures the intended logic more clearly:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; this.get(i+1) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This ensures that for each element from the given index to the old size minus one, the element at the next position is either `null` if the current element is `null`, or it remains unchanged.
